.\"                                      Hey, EMACS: -*- nroff -*-
.TH MOSH 1 "July 2026"
.SH NAME
mosh-ssh \- OpenSSH-compatible entrypoint backed by Mosh forwarding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mosh-ssh
[\-T]
[\-N]
[\-D [\fIBIND_ADDRESS\fP:]\fIPORT\fP]
[\-L [\fIBIND_ADDRESS\fP:]\fIPORT\fP:\fIHOST\fP:\fIHOSTPORT\fP]
[\fIssh-options\fP]
[user@]host
[command...]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmosh-ssh\fP is an SSH-compatible setup command for tools that expect
to launch an \fBssh\fP executable, including VS Code Remote-SSH. It uses
ordinary SSH only for authentication and to start
.BR mosh-server (1)
in stdio forwarding mode. After bootstrap, command stdio and local
forwarding traffic run over an encrypted Mosh UDP forwarding sidecar.

This command is intentionally a small OpenSSH subset. It is meant for
non-interactive command stdio and local forwarding, not for replacing
interactive
.BR mosh (1).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-T
Accepted for OpenSSH compatibility. \fBmosh-ssh\fP never requests a
remote PTY.

.TP
.B \-N
Do not run a remote command. This is useful for forwarding-only
sessions.

.TP
.B \-D [\fIBIND_ADDRESS\fP:]\fIPORT\fP
Listen on a local TCP port and run a SOCKS5 no-authentication CONNECT
proxy over Mosh forwarding. Domain names are resolved on the server
side. If \fIBIND_ADDRESS\fP is omitted, bind to 127.0.0.1.

.TP
.B \-L [\fIBIND_ADDRESS\fP:]\fIPORT\fP:\fIHOST\fP:\fIHOSTPORT\fP
Listen on a local TCP port and forward accepted connections over Mosh
forwarding to \fIHOST\fP:\fIHOSTPORT\fP from the server side. If
\fIBIND_ADDRESS\fP is omitted, bind to 127.0.0.1.

.TP
.B \-p \fIPORT\fP
Pass the SSH bootstrap port to \fBssh\fP.

.TP
.B \-l \fIUSER\fP
Pass the SSH bootstrap user to \fBssh\fP.

.TP
.B \-F \fICONFIG\fP, \-i \fIIDENTITY_FILE\fP, \-J \fIJUMP\fP, \-o \fIKEY=VALUE\fP
Pass common OpenSSH options through to the bootstrap \fBssh\fP command.

.TP
.B \-\-local
Run \fBmosh-server\fP locally instead of using SSH. This is intended for
testing.

.SH VS CODE
To use \fBmosh-ssh\fP with VS Code Remote-SSH, install compatible
\fBmosh-ssh\fP and \fBmosh-client\fP locally and compatible
\fBmosh-server\fP on the remote host, then set:

.nf
{
  "remote.SSH.path": "/path/to/mosh-ssh",
  "remote.SSH.enableDynamicForwarding": true,
  "remote.SSH.remoteServerListenOnSocket": false
}
.fi

The socket listen mode should be disabled for this milestone because
\fBmosh-ssh\fP currently supports TCP forwarding, not Unix-domain socket
forwarding.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B MOSH_SERVER
Path to the \fBmosh-server\fP executable to start during bootstrap.
This is mostly useful for testing or staged installs.

.SH LIMITATIONS
\fBmosh-ssh\fP does not support remote forwarding (\fB\-R\fP), X11
forwarding, SSH agent forwarding, ControlMaster, Unix-domain socket
forwarding, or the full OpenSSH configuration language.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mosh (1),
.BR mosh-client (1),
.BR mosh-server (1),
.BR ssh (1).
